body:
SET_STREAM_INFO for a Stream Output currently accepts only the IEEE 1722.1-2021 command body, the 84-byte form of Figure 7-40 (control_data_length 96), which Milan v1.2 5.4.2.9 references. A command with the IEEE 1722.1-2013 48-byte body (control_data_length 60) is answered BAD_ARGUMENTS with a zeroed 84-byte body, whatever its values and even when the output is stopped (`hdl/aecp/KL_aecp_engine.sv`, the SET_STREAM_INFO arm). Controllers and tools that still send the 2013 form therefore cannot set the presentation-time offset.

Owner decision 2026-10-17: the end station must support Milan and IEEE 1722.1, so both forms are accepted.

Done when:
- SET_STREAM_INFO accepts the 2013 48-byte body and the 2021 84-byte body, with the same field semantics, the same MSRP_ACC_LAT_VALID-only rule, the same refusal while streaming, and BAD_ARGUMENTS for a bad value;
- the response always uses the 2021 form;
- a suite case covers each length, including a short body that is neither form, which must still be refused;
- the processor's suites and the parent's consumer gates pass.
